# Template for the operator account's authorized_keys (G3-02). Bootstrap replaces the placeholder with the public key of the
# deploy key for one environment. The public key is not in the repo. The command= option forces the wrapper with the bound
# environment as its argument. restrict turns on every restriction, which includes these, so the key cannot get a shell,
# a terminal, port forwarding, agent forwarding, X11, a user rc file or any other option: no-pty, no-port-forwarding,
# no-agent-forwarding, no-X11-forwarding, no-user-rc. The command path is the install path of the wrapper.
# Do not put a real key in this file. One line per environment, with <ENVIRONMENT> replaced by that environment's name.
command="/usr/local/libexec/geldar-deploy/channel <ENVIRONMENT>",restrict ssh-ed25519 <PUBLIC_KEY_PLACEHOLDER> geldar-deploy-<ENVIRONMENT>
